From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdi32: the engine services a printer maker's driver imports

Printer makers ship their Windows drivers as printer graphics DLLs (Zebra's
ZDesigner, Brother's QL and laser drivers, Epson's inkjet drivers all
export DrvEnableDriver), which import GDI's engine services from gdi32:
EngCreateBitmap, EngAssociateSurface, EngWritePrinter, the XXXOBJ_ helpers.
Wine's gdi32 had none, so such a driver did not even load. This adds them,
written from the DDI documentation, with the declarations they need
(include/ddk/winddi.h, and include/wine/printdrv.h for the Unidrv plug-in
interfaces and what a print processor hosting a driver tells gdi32):
surfaces are plain bitmaps a print processor draws the pages into,
EngWritePrinter sends the driver's output to the job's port (or a file, for
our 64-bit host), copies and solid fills are done, and the drawing services
answer that they drew nothing, which a driver takes as a drawing it could
not do.

Test: test/printdrv-gate.sh with test/printdrv-umpd.c, test/printdrv-plugin.c
and test/printdrv-probe.c (mutant SG_MUTANT_ENGWRITE).
---
--- a/dlls/gdi32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/gdi32/Makefile.in
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	objects.c \
 	opengl.c \
 	text.c \
+	umpd.c \
 	uniscribe/bidi.c \
 	uniscribe/bracket.c \
 	uniscribe/breaking.c \
